See LICENSE for the complete license text.

Summary of modifications (2026):
- replaced the launcher's screens with a dedicated digital-audio-player
  interface for the Sony NW-ZX1, in a late-1990s Sony portable-audio
  design language (an STN-LCD glass set into a graphite chassis, with
  an amber TUBE AMP alternate style), on a reproducible,
  dependency-free API 16 build;
- added a now-playing layer that reads the playing track, play state,
  timing, and audio format live from the firmware player's service
  binder and Sony's media database (this firmware broadcasts no
  metadata), rendering the track's album art in period LCD tones or
  full color and scrolling long titles MiniDisc-deck style;
- added an in-launcher music library browser (playlists / artists /
  albums / songs) over the firmware's media database, cached for
  instant opens and refreshed by a short-lived broadcast-triggered
  background service, which starts playback on the firmware player
  through the player's own binder protocol without leaving the
  launcher;
- added launcher-owned playlists stored as playlists in Android's own
  media database, so each list is simultaneously a stored list and a
  real playback queue the firmware player accepts - create, rename,
  delete, add, remove, play from any track, and append to the playing
  queue without interrupting playback;
- brought the chassis spectrum window to life without audio capture
  (impossible on this hardware): a lowest-priority background service
  analyzes each track once, on its first play, into a small stored
  envelope replayed in sync with the player's own clock, carrying
  original ALAC and FLAC decoders written from the published format
  specifications for the formats the firmware's Android media stack
  cannot decode;
- added a storage readout for USB mass storage: home, the library and
  the playlists say when the computer holds the music volume, offer a
  key that ends USB storage, and show the firmware's reindex and the
  launcher's library rebuild before the normal screens return, while
  playback and playlist edits are refused until the volume is back.

